{"complete":true,"city":"Chongqing","template_id":"global-first-24-hours","title":"Your First 24 Hours in Chongqing, Dealt as Cards","description":"A first-day sequence that reads Chongqing through breakfast noodles, cliff-hugging transit, civic collections, migration architecture, a river crossing, hotpot, and an illuminated hillside finale.","icon":"schedule","cards":[{"entity_name":"Yu Xiaomian","title":"Yu Xiaomian","subtitle":"Breakfast: begin with the city’s everyday bowl","notes":"Order xiaomian with or without broth; the source identifies both as established forms of Chongqing noodles.","short_summary":"Yu Xiaomian’s noodle maker begins each day by kneading fresh dough, while the shop’s seasonings draw together chilies, preserved vegetables, mustard greens, and Sichuan peppercorns. It gives the morning a concrete introduction to the careful assembly behind an apparently simple bowl.","source_url":"https://www.ichongqing.info/2020/12/04/xiaomian-chongqing-noodles-chongqing-delicacies-animation-series/amp/","source_title":"Xiaomian (Chongqing Noodles) | Chongqing Delicacies Animation Series","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Liziba Observation Deck","title":"Liziba Observation Deck","subtitle":"Orientation: watch infrastructure meet the hillside","notes":"Stand outside the station and watch Line 2 trains pass through the adjoining building.","short_summary":"The observation deck faces Liziba Station, where Chongqing Rail Transit Line 2 passes through a 19-story building. It is a quick visual lesson in how ordinary infrastructure negotiates the city’s steep, densely built terrain.","source_url":"https://global.chinadaily.com.cn/a/202606/15/WS6a2bef4aa310986e2b45fac5.html","source_title":"Chongqing's Liziba Station is on everyone's 'must-eat' list","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Huangguan Escalator","title":"Huangguan Escalator","subtitle":"Transit lesson: change elevation the Chongqing way","notes":"The escalator is also called the Chongqing Crown Escalator.","short_summary":"This long single-flight escalator links the Lianglukou transit area with Caiyuanba below. Rather than treating the slope as scenery, the stop shows how Chongqing turns a major elevation change into part of the transport network.","source_url":"https://www.chinadaily.com.cn/a/202203/16/WS62319511a310fd2b29e51481_1.html","source_title":"Chongqing's super long escalator back in service","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Chongqing China Three Gorges Museum","title":"Chongqing China Three Gorges Museum","subtitle":"Context: place the city inside its river region","notes":"Choose among the permanent displays on the Three Gorges, ancient Bayu, Chongqing’s urban development, and the wartime years.","short_summary":"The museum’s collections connect Bayu culture, the Three Gorges, migration, wartime history, and Chongqing’s growth as a city. This is the day’s evidence room: objects and exhibitions supply context for the riverfront and historic districts encountered later.","source_url":"https://english.cq.gov.cn/aboutchongqing/culture/Museums/202606/t20260613_15751582.html","source_title":"Chongqing China Three Gorges Museum","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Chongqing People's Square","title":"Chongqing People's Square","subtitle":"Pause: read the city’s civic composition","notes":"Step outside the museum and observe how the square arranges the museum and Great Hall of the People as one ensemble.","short_summary":"Chongqing’s government describes the square, Three Gorges Museum, and adjacent Great Hall of the People as a landmark urban cultural complex. The open space provides a useful pause for reading those institutions together rather than as isolated buildings.","source_url":"https://english.cq.gov.cn/aboutchongqing/culture/Museums/202606/t20260613_15751582.html","source_title":"Chongqing China Three Gorges Museum","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"People's Liberation Monument","title":"People's Liberation Monument","subtitle":"City center: locate downtown around a wartime memorial","notes":"Look beyond the surrounding retail towers: the monument’s commemorative purpose predates the present commercial district.","short_summary":"Commonly called Jiefangbei, the monument was completed in 1947 and renamed in 1950. It now anchors Chongqing’s central business district, placing a wartime memorial at the point from which the surrounding pedestrian city radiates.","source_url":"https://english.cq.gov.cn/latestnews/Editor/202606/t20260608_15735957.html","source_title":"Cinematic Chongqing: A Walk Through Yuzhong District, Where History Flows and Movies Live","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Chongqing Huguang Guild Hall","title":"Chongqing Huguang Guild Hall","subtitle":"Migration story: inspect the institutions merchants built","notes":"Give attention to the carved and painted beams of Emperor Yu’s Palace and the inscribed plaques.","short_summary":"The guild complex was built during the Ming and Qing periods as a meeting place for merchants from Hunan, Hubei, Guangdong, and Guangxi. Its halls make Chongqing’s history of trade and inward migration legible in timber, ornament, and inscriptions.","source_url":"https://www.chinadaily.com.cn/china/2007-04/21/content_856382_3.htm","source_title":"Huguang guild buildings in Chongqing","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Yangtze River Cableway","title":"Yangtze River Cableway","subtitle":"River crossing: exchange the street grid for an aerial view","notes":"Treat the ride as surviving transport infrastructure as well as a viewpoint.","short_summary":"Launched in 1987, the cableway crosses the Yangtze in cars whose later design retained the original model’s visual character. Once a routine way for residents to move through the mountain city, it offers a direct look at the river corridor shaping downtown.","source_url":"https://global.chinadaily.com.cn/a/201912/23/WS5e001c56a310cf3e3557febb.html","source_title":"Iconic Yangtze cableway in SW China reopens after upgrade","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Dezhuang 1898 Cultural Experience Center","title":"Dezhuang 1898 Cultural Experience Center","subtitle":"Dinner: negotiate the hotpot’s heat together","notes":"The sourced branch is at No. 21 Danzishi Old Street in Nan’an District. Ask about the available spice level instead of assuming one fixed broth.","short_summary":"Dezhuang documents Chongqing hotpot broths in several heat levels and developed a quantified scale intended to make those differences clearer. At its Danzishi Old Street branch, dinner becomes a shared exercise in choosing a broth and cooking ingredients at the table.","source_url":"https://www.ichongqing.info/restaurant/dezhuang-hot-pot/amp/","source_title":"Dezhuang Hot Pot","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Hongya Cave","title":"Hongya Cave","subtitle":"Nightcap: finish inside a stacked version of the old city","notes":"Seek the fifth-floor street installation, designed around scenes of Chongqing life in the 1980s.","short_summary":"Hongya Cave’s fifth-floor themed street reconstructs settings such as tube-shaped apartments, a fruit market, old roads, a tram, and Chongqing Station. After a day of real slopes and layered transport, its staged cityscape offers a self-conscious account of how Chongqing remembers its recent street life.","source_url":"https://www.ichongqing.info/2020/08/18/new-destination-in-hongya-cave-restores-chongqings-street-in-1980s/","source_title":"New Destination in Hongya Cave: Restores Chongqing's Street in 1980s","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null}],"warnings":["The input contained no candidate places. Consequently, all place_id, maps_url, latitude, and longitude fields are null.","Venue operations and exhibits can change; this board intentionally makes no current-hours, admission, or journey-duration claims."]}
